## 🎯 HOW TO USE THESE PROMPTS

### Step 1: Prepare Your Environment
```bash
# Create a development branch
git checkout -b refactor/production-restructure

# Create the directory structure
mkdir -p src/{config,constants,types,hooks,services,utils,middleware,store,components/common,components/features,pages,layouts,routes,styles,assets,lib}
mkdir -p tests/{unit,integration,e2e}
mkdir -p docs
```

### Step 2: Execute Phase by Phase

For each phase:
1. Copy the relevant PHASE prompt
2. Share it with Claude or your AI assistant
3. Follow the generated instructions
4. Test the implementation
5. Move to next phase

### Step 3: Validation Checklist

After each phase, verify:
```bash
# Phase 1
✓ Path aliases work correctly
✓ Environment variables load properly
✓ TypeScript compilation successful

# Phase 2
✓ API client makes requests
✓ Services can be imported
✓ No console errors

# Phase 3
✓ Components render without errors
✓ Styles apply correctly
✓ All props are typed

# Phase 4
✓ Redux store initializes
✓ Actions dispatch successfully
✓ Selectors return correct data

# Phase 5
✓ Routes navigate properly
✓ Protected routes work
✓ Layouts render

# Phase 6
✓ Tests run without errors
✓ Coverage is 80%+
✓ Mocks work correctly

# Phase 7
✓ Documentation is complete
✓ All links work
✓ Examples are accurate
```

### Step 4: Code Review Checklist

- [ ] No TypeScript errors
- [ ] All imports use path aliases
- [ ] Code follows naming conventions
- [ ] Components are properly typed
- [ ] Tests are passing
- [ ] No console errors/warnings
- [ ] Performance is acceptable
- [ ] Security best practices followed

